PMID- 42128763
OWN - NLM
STAT- Publisher
LR  - 20260513
IS  - 1557-8259 (Electronic)
IS  - 0030-6665 (Linking)
DP  - 2026 May 13
TI  - Advanced/Novel Stenting for Pediatric Dynamic Airway Collapse.
LID - S0030-6665(26)00057-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.otc.2026.03.030 [doi]
AB  - Pediatric dynamic airway collapse is a complex condition that can impact all 
      levels of the pediatric airway. These conditions can pose life threatening risk 
      to pediatric patients and carry lasting impacts. While traditionally, 
      tracheostomy has been used to address all levels of dynamic collapse, recent 
      advances have allowed for more individualized, anatomy-specific stenting and 
      splinting strategies for treatment. This article covers pathophysiology and the 
      latest evidence on strategies to address nasopharyngeal, oropharyngeal, proximal 
      trachea, and tracheobronchial dynamic collapse.
