TI  - Hybrid Tracheal Stent Ingestion in Malignant Central Airway Stenosis: A Case 
      Report.
PG  - e70329
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.70329 [doi]
LID - e70329
AB  - Airway stents provide symptomatic relief in malignant central airway stenosis, 
      but carry the risk of migration, which may result in potentially lethal stent 
      ingestion. A 22-year-old man underwent hybrid stent placement for 
      tracheobronchial stenosis caused by an undiagnosed large mediastinal mass. Within 
      3 weeks after placement, following initial chemotherapy for provisionally 
      diagnosed B-cell lymphoma, the stent migrated and was ingested. The stent was 
      successfully retrieved endoscopically. This is the first reported case of hybrid 
      tracheal stent ingestion. Early surveillance is warranted in patients with 
      anticipated tumour regression.
