TI  - Successful stent removal after chemoradiotherapy followed by durvalumab for 
      locally advanced non-small cell lung cancer with airway stenosis: A report of 
      three cases.
PG  - 102217
LID - 10.1016/j.rmcr.2025.102217 [doi]
LID - 102217
AB  - Airway stents improve respiratory conditions and Eastern Cooperative Oncology 
      Group Performance Status scores in cases of airway stenosis, as observed in 
      patients with stage III non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) who experience 
      prolonged survival after undergoing chemoradiotherapy followed by durvalumab 
      treatment. Herein, we report three cases of severe airway stenosis due to stage 
      III NSCLC in patients who underwent airway stenting and subsequent stent removal 
      after chemoradiotherapy and durvalumab administration. The number of stents 
      removed will likely increase in the future due to the high response rates to 
      molecular drugs and immune checkpoint inhibitors.
