TI  - Successful Therapy of 2 Esophagobronchial-Tracheal Fistulas After Esophagectomy 
      by Endoscopic Vacuum Therapy and Bronchial Stenting.
PG  - 283-287
LID - 10.1016/j.atssr.2025.09.016 [doi]
AB  - Development of an esophagobronchial-tracheal fistula is a rare but severe 
      complication of esophagectomy. There is no standardized treatment. We present the 
      cases of 2 patients with esophagobronchial-tracheal fistulas after anastomotic 
      leakage after esophagectomy with gastric tube reconstruction. We successfully 
      treated these fistulas by implanting covered airway stents and by performing 
      simultaneous esophageal endoscopic vacuum therapy (EVT). As a precondition for 
      EVT, we provided a solution for compartmentalization between the wound cavity and 
      the tracheobronchial system by performing bronchial-tracheal stenting and 
      esophageal EVT in both cases. We propose a minimally invasive therapeutic 
      alternative in the therapy of esophagobronchial-tracheal fistula after 
      esophagectomy.
